# mail/components/unifiedtoolbar/modules/CustomizableItemsDetails.mjs: grouped behavior record

Coverage: complete. Product tests were not run by this pipeline.

Source context: {"language":"JavaScript","runtime":"privileged Thunderbird module or xpcshell harness","role":"source","component":"mail/unifiedtoolbar"}

## module top-level imports, exports, state, registrations and data (module-top-level)

Exports a mutable array of50 customization descriptors. Universal entries have absent/empty spaces; mail, calendar/tasks, calendar-only and addressbook entries restrict availability. spacer alone allows repetition; spacer/search-bar/throbber skip focus. Fields choose preview label, wrapper CSS class, live template and module imports. The exact per-entry mappings and verified companion anchors are retained as relationships. This contract ends at the template/control binding; command-handler implementation bodies are outside this data-module scope.

- reads: Literal IDs, labels, spaces, template IDs, module URI arrays and flag values for50items.
- writes: Creates one exported array and its descriptor objects/arrays at module evaluation; no runtime state changes.
- branches: No executable condition in the catalog. Consumer eligibility branches use spaces/flags as described in catalog-consumer.
- result: Default-exported shared descriptor array.
- errors: No runtime validation in this data module; an unknown item ID causes the consumer to throw, and failed dynamic imports reject its initializer.
- async: Synchronous unless this unit explicitly describes await; observer waits do not certify completion of all observers or UI imports.
- ownership: The module owns the mutable descriptor array; CustomizableElement retains a descriptor reference as this.details.

Evidence anchors: [{"sourceId":"thunderbird:mail/components/unifiedtoolbar/modules/CustomizableItemsDetails.mjs","start":1,"end":482}]. Shared contracts: ["catalog-consumer"].

